#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:52
msgid ""
"If you want a template listener to be used by all styles, it should be "
"placed in the ``all/`` style directory, e.g. ``vendor/extname/styles/all/"
"template/event/``. This helps prevent code duplication and eases style file "
"management."
msgstr ""
"If you want a template listener to be used by all styles, it should be "
"placed in the ``all/`` style directory, e.g. ``vendor/extname/styles/all/"
"template/event/``. This helps prevent code duplication and eases style file "
"management."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:56
msgid ""
"The prosilver and subsilver2 directories should be used for template files "
"that must be custom tailored to each style. Similarly, if a 3rd-party style "
"requires additional customisation to maintain compatibility, a folder for "
"that style should be included with those template files."
msgstr ""
"The prosilver and subsilver2 directories should be used for template files "
"that must be custom tailored to each style. Similarly, if a 3rd-party style "
"requires additional customisation to maintain compatibility, a folder for "
"that style should be included with those template files."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:61
msgid ""
"To add ACP template listeners, place those files in ``vendor/extname/adm/"
"style/event/``."
msgstr ""
"To add ACP template listeners, place those files in ``vendor/extname/adm/"
"style/event/``."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:63
msgid ""
"Inside the template listener, we will create a nav-bar link. This consists "
"of a simple list element, with a link and a description:"
msgstr ""
"Inside the template listener, we will create a nav-bar link. This consists "
"of a simple list element, with a link and a description:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:74
msgid ""
"Once the template listener has been created, you should be able to see the "
"new link in the board's nav-bar, with the icon of the FAQ link and the text "
"``DEMO_PAGE``. We will fix the link text in the next section."
msgstr ""
"Once the template listener has been created, you should be able to see the "
"new link in the board's nav-bar, with the icon of the FAQ link and the text "
"``DEMO_PAGE``. We will fix the link text in the next section."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:80
msgid ""
"If the link does not appear, you may need to purge the board cache from the "
"main page of the ACP. You can also enable ``DEBUG_MODE`` in your ``config."
"php`` file, which will force the template engine to always look for template "
"listeners when a page is being rendered."
msgstr ""
"If the link does not appear, you may need to purge the board cache from the "
"main page of the ACP. You can also enable ``DEBUG_MODE`` in your ``config."
"php`` file, which will force the template engine to always look for template "
"listeners when a page is being rendered."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:85
msgid ""
"It's important to understand that when phpBB compiles the templates, there "
"is no current system for determining the priority in which template "
"listeners from different extensions subscribed to the same event are "
"compiled. In rare cases some extensions could cause a conflict, in which "
"case the recommendation is for the extension authors to work together on a "
"solution for their conflicting template listeners."
msgstr ""
"It's important to understand that when phpBB compiles the templates, there "
"is no current system for determining the priority in which template "
"listeners from different extensions subscribed to the same event are "
"compiled. In rare cases some extensions could cause a conflict, in which "
"case the recommendation is for the extension authors to work together on a "
"solution for their conflicting template listeners."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:94
msgid "PHP Core Events & Listeners"
msgstr "PHP Core Events & Listeners"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:96
msgid ""
"Events allow extensions to execute code in many locations within core phpBB "
"code, without modifying any of the code. That way extensions can easily add "
"features, remove functionality or modify behaviour, while maintaining "
"compatibility and simple update procedures."
msgstr ""
"Events allow extensions to execute code in many locations within core phpBB "
"code, without modifying any of the code. That way extensions can easily add "
"features, remove functionality or modify behaviour, while maintaining "
"compatibility and simple update procedures."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:102
msgid "Terminology"
msgstr "Terminology"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:104
msgid "Events"
msgstr "Events"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:105
msgid ""
"Events are dispatched at various places in the core phpBB code. Listeners in "
"extensions subscribe to these events. They are able to execute code whenever "
"the respective event has occurred. An alternative name for events is “hook "
"locations”."
msgstr ""
"Events are dispatched at various places in the core phpBB code. Listeners in "
"extensions subscribe to these events. They are able to execute code whenever "
"the respective event has occurred. An alternative name for events is “hook "
"locations”."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:109
msgid "Listeners"
msgstr "Listeners"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:110
msgid ""
"Listeners are triggered by events. They are methods that can process "
"incoming data and manipulate variables in the scope of the event. So they "
"can change phpBB's behaviour, add new functionality or if used in the "
"context of templates, modify the output. Numerous listeners form part of a "
"subscriber. An alternative name for listeners is \"hooks\"."
msgstr ""
"Listeners are triggered by events. They are methods that can process "
"incoming data and manipulate variables in the scope of the event. So they "
"can change phpBB's behaviour, add new functionality or if used in the "
"context of templates, modify the output. Numerous listeners form part of a "
"subscriber. An alternative name for listeners is \"hooks\"."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:118
msgid ""
"View the full list of supported `PHP events <https://area51.phpbb.com/docs/"
"dev/3.3.x/extensions/events_list.html#php-events>`_."
msgstr ""
"View the full list of supported `PHP events <https://area51.phpbb.com/docs/"
"dev/3.3.x/extensions/events_list.html#php-events>`_."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:121
msgid "The event listener"
msgstr "The event listener"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:123
msgid ""
"In the previous section we created a template listener that adds a link for "
"the Acme Demo extension to phpBB's nav-bar. We will now use PHP events to "
"load a language file that contains the ``DEMO_PAGE`` language key so that "
"our nav-bar link will display with the correct text."
msgstr ""
"In the previous section we created a template listener that adds a link for "
"the Acme Demo extension to phpBB's nav-bar. We will now use PHP events to "
"load a language file that contains the ``DEMO_PAGE`` language key so that "
"our nav-bar link will display with the correct text."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:128
msgid ""
"To do so, we need to create a PHP event listener class (a.k.a. subscriber "
"class). This class includes a set of listener methods, each of which can "
"*subscribe* to PHP events in phpBB's codebase. The listener class must be "
"created in the ``event/`` subdirectory of the extension directory or it will "
"not work. It must also conform to the following requirements:"
msgstr ""
"To do so, we need to create a PHP event listener class (a.k.a. subscriber "
"class). This class includes a set of listener methods, each of which can "
"*subscribe* to PHP events in phpBB's codebase. The listener class must be "
"created in the ``event/`` subdirectory of the extension directory or it will "
"not work. It must also conform to the following requirements:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:134
msgid ""
"Follow extension class name-spacing conventions: "
"``vendor\\extname\\event\\subscribername.php``."
msgstr ""
"Follow extension class name-spacing conventions: "
"``vendor\\extname\\event\\subscribername.php``."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:135
msgid ""
"Implement Symfony's "
"``Symfony\\Component\\EventDispatcher\\EventSubscriberInterface`` interface."
msgstr ""
"Implement Symfony's "
"``Symfony\\Component\\EventDispatcher\\EventSubscriberInterface`` interface."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:137
msgid ""
"Use the static method ``getSubscribedEvents()`` to subscribe methods in the "
"listener to specific events, the keys of which contain event names and the "
"values of which contain listener function names."
msgstr ""
"Use the static method ``getSubscribedEvents()`` to subscribe methods in the "
"listener to specific events, the keys of which contain event names and the "
"values of which contain listener function names."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:141
msgid ""
"In the Acme Demo extension, we want to load our language file everywhere. "
"Therefore we will subscribe a listener function to phpBB's ``core."
"user_setup`` event:"
msgstr ""
"In the Acme Demo extension, we want to load our language file everywhere. "
"Therefore we will subscribe a listener function to phpBB's ``core."
"user_setup`` event:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:183
msgid "So what is the ``main_listener.php`` class above actually doing?"
msgstr "So what is the ``main_listener.php`` class above actually doing?"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:185
msgid ""
"The ``getSubscribedEvents()`` method is subscribing our listener function "
"``load_language_on_setup()`` to the event named ``core.user_setup``. This "
"means that when this event occurs, our function will execute."
msgstr ""
"The ``getSubscribedEvents()`` method is subscribing our listener function "
"``load_language_on_setup()`` to the event named ``core.user_setup``. This "
"means that when this event occurs, our function will execute."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:191
msgid ""
"You can assign multiple listener functions to a single event using an array:"
msgstr ""
"You can assign multiple listener functions to a single event using an array:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:197
msgid ""
"The ``load_language_on_setup()`` listener method simply adds our language "
"file to phpBB's language data array. Generally speaking, a listener is "
"simply a public function in the subscriber class, referred to in the array "
"returned by ``getSubscribedEvents()``. It takes one argument, ``$event``. "
"This parameter allows you to access and modify the variables that are given "
"to the event from the core code. In this case we are modifying the "
"``lang_set_ext`` variable by adding Acme Demo's language file to it."
msgstr ""
"The ``load_language_on_setup()`` listener method simply adds our language "
"file to phpBB's language data array. Generally speaking, a listener is "
"simply a public function in the subscriber class, referred to in the array "
"returned by ``getSubscribedEvents()``. It takes one argument, ``$event``. "
"This parameter allows you to access and modify the variables that are given "
"to the event from the core code. In this case we are modifying the "
"``lang_set_ext`` variable by adding Acme Demo's language file to it."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:207
msgid ""
"Note how the ``lang_set_ext`` event variable is first copied by assigning it "
"to a local variable, then modified, and then copied back. This shortcut does "
"not work: ``$event['foo']['bar'] = $baz;`` This is because the event "
"variables are overloaded, which is a limitation in PHP."
msgstr ""
"Note how the ``lang_set_ext`` event variable is first copied by assigning it "
"to a local variable, then modified, and then copied back. This shortcut does "
"not work: ``$event['foo']['bar'] = $baz;`` This is because the event "
"variables are overloaded, which is a limitation in PHP."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:213
msgid "Registering the listener"
msgstr "Registering the listener"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:215
msgid ""
"To have phpBB autoload and execute our event listener class, we need to "
"create a service definition for it. This is done by creating a ``config/"
"services.yml`` file in the extension:"
msgstr ""
"To have phpBB autoload and execute our event listener class, we need to "
"create a service definition for it. This is done by creating a ``config/"
"services.yml`` file in the extension:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:229
msgid ""
"YAML files are indentation sensitive. They require an indentation size of 4 "
"spaces per indent, **do not use tabs**."
msgstr ""
"YAML files are indentation sensitive. They require an indentation size of 4 "
"spaces per indent, **do not use tabs**."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:232
msgid ""
"The first line tells phpBB that a list of services is being registered. On "
"the next line we specify the name of the service, which is for our event "
"listener in this case."
msgstr ""
"The first line tells phpBB that a list of services is being registered. On "
"the next line we specify the name of the service, which is for our event "
"listener in this case."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:238
msgid "Service names must be prefixed with your vendor and extension name."
msgstr "Service names must be prefixed with your vendor and extension name."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:240
msgid ""
"The ``class`` attribute must contain the name-space and class name of the "
"service being registered. The name-space depends on the file's location, "
"within the ``ext/`` directory. Thus, the file ``ext/acme/demo/event/"
"main_listener.php`` has the namespace ``acme\\demo\\event`` and class name "
"``main_listener``. The full name of the class is therefore "
"``acme\\demo\\event\\main_listener`` which is what we need to specify here."
msgstr ""
"The ``class`` attribute must contain the name-space and class name of the "
"service being registered. The name-space depends on the file's location, "
"within the ``ext/`` directory. Thus, the file ``ext/acme/demo/event/"
"main_listener.php`` has the namespace ``acme\\demo\\event`` and class name "
"``main_listener``. The full name of the class is therefore "
"``acme\\demo\\event\\main_listener`` which is what we need to specify here."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:247
msgid ""
"The ``tags`` attribute tells phpBB that the service is an event listener."
msgstr ""
"The ``tags`` attribute tells phpBB that the service is an event listener."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:249
msgid ""
"Once the services YAML file has been created (or modified), phpBB's cache "
"needs to be purged. After purging the cache in the ACP, the description of "
"the link in the navigation bar should now display ``Demo`` instead of "
"``DEMO_PAGE``."
msgstr ""
"Once the services YAML file has been created (or modified), phpBB's cache "
"needs to be purged. After purging the cache in the ACP, the description of "
"the link in the navigation bar should now display ``Demo`` instead of "
"``DEMO_PAGE``."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:256
msgid ""
"phpBB’s core PHP and template files have been prepared with dozens of event "
"locations. However, if there are no events where your extension may need "
"one, the phpBB development team welcomes event requests at the `area51.com "
"Event Requests <https://area51.phpbb.com/phpBB/viewforum.php?f=111>`_ forum."
msgstr ""
"phpBB’s core PHP and template files have been prepared with dozens of event "
"locations. However, if there are no events where your extension may need "
"one, the phpBB development team welcomes event requests at the `area51.com "
"Event Requests <https://area51.phpbb.com/phpBB/viewforum.php?f=111>`_ forum."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:262
msgid "Prioritising event listeners (optional)"
msgstr "Prioritising event listeners (optional)"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:264
msgid ""
"Sometimes different extensions can run into problems when competing for use "
"of the same PHP core events. In trying to resolve these issues, the "
"extension developer may want to prioritise their extension over others, so "
"that their extension will be triggered before other extensions."
msgstr ""
"Sometimes different extensions can run into problems when competing for use "
"of the same PHP core events. In trying to resolve these issues, the "
"extension developer may want to prioritise their extension over others, so "
"that their extension will be triggered before other extensions."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:269
msgid ""
"In such cases, the ``getSubscribedEvents()`` method provides an argument for "
"setting a priority for event listener methods. For example:"
msgstr ""
"In such cases, the ``getSubscribedEvents()`` method provides an argument for "
"setting a priority for event listener methods. For example:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_events.rst:281
msgid ""
"In this example, ``$priority`` is an integer, the value of which defaults to "
"0. Setting this integer to higher values equals more importance and "
"therefore that listener will be triggered earlier than others subscribed to "
"this event."
msgstr ""
"In this example, ``$priority`` is an integer, the value of which defaults to "
"0. Setting this integer to higher values equals more importance and "
"therefore that listener will be triggered earlier than others subscribed to "
"this event."

